{
    "architecture": "x86_64",
    "context": "Native affinity import/query and stable-peer permission contract: 49416 root/UID1000 checks per architecture, eight target classes, 19 unsigned32 lengths, ten guarded input/output forms, upper PID/length words and real musl affinity wrappers. Short zero-extended masks, unsigned32 getter bit-count overflow, error ordering, live worker TIDs and UID1001 target with CAP_SYS_NICE off/on. Exact masks/guards, ignored inaccessible tails, restoration, original failure vectors and identical-ELF Linux 6.12.51 references. Twenty probe allocas; two flat warmed 200-cycle cohorts. Four production builds, exact complete C scope, eight-case profiles, compiler/source/C/ELF/reference pins, executing auditor negative controls and independent lifetime review. Large masks/CPU hotplug, ARM CPU1 QoS, credential/TID races, namespaces/pledge, GNU/foreign/ELF32 and broad roadmap gates remain separate",
